silm:instances_papers_11_base_commutative_diagram_chapters_26_circuit_imprint_tensor_sections_02_eight_corners_atlas_concrete_anchor_1#corner_001 silm:hasLongDescription "The Corner_001 is [virtual, class, evidential]: logician with class-level evidence chains -- Cat-implies-Mammal as a deduction step. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'Corner_001', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
